-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Nov  5 00:48:39 UTC 2026 - Steve Kowalik <steven.kowalik@suse.com>

- Update to 6.2.0.post2:
  * MAJOR REWRITE: The Python and C implementations of the encoder and
    decoder were replaced with a single, Rust-based implementation in the
    interest of maintainability. Highlights include improved memory safety
    (100% safe-mode Rust), complete elimination of reference leaks, support
    for free-threading and subinterpreters, substantially improved
    performance, improved decoder error handling where any non-base
    exception gets wrapped in a CBORDecodeError, and iterative rather than
    recursive decoding so container nesting depth is limited only by
    available memory rather than the C stack size.
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Changed the signature of the tag_hook decoder
    callables to accept (CBORTag, immutable) as arguments instead of
    (CBORDecoder, CBORTag).
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Changed the signature of the object_hook decoder
    callables to accept (Mapping[Any, Any], bool) instead of (CBORDecoder,
    dict[Any, Any]).
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Removed the break_marker singleton as no longer
    necessary.
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Removed the CBORDecodeValueError exception,
    instead chaining ValueError or TypeError to a CBORDecodeError.
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Changed the decoding of semantic tag 261 to yield
    an IPv4Interface or IPv6Interface if the address contains host bits.
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Removed the individual decoding functions from
    the API as they were mistakenly called directly by users.
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Changed the encoding of IP addresses to use the
    semantic tags 52 and 54 instead of the deprecated 260 and 261.
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Dropped the deprecated cbor2.decoder and
    cbor2.encoder modules; everything in the API is now importable directly
    from cbor2.
  * BACKWARD INCOMPATIBLE: Renamed the cbor2.FrozenDict class to frozendict
    (not available on Python 3.15 where the built-in frozendict class must
    be used instead).
  * Dropped support for Python 3.9.
  * Added the semantic_decoders decoder option to add or override decoders
    for specific semantic tags.
  * Added the immutable decoder flag to always use immutable containers
    where possible when decoding a CBOR stream.
  * Added the allow_indefinite decoder option to optionally disallow
    indefinite-length strings and containers.
  * Added the allow_duplicate_keys parameter to CBORDecoder, load() and
    loads() (default: True) to raise a CBORDecodeError upon encountering a
    duplicate key within the same map.
  * Added support for decoding from any object supporting the buffer API
    (e.g. memoryview or bytearray) in addition to bytes.
  * Added the strict_hashable_types parameter to CBORDecoder, load() and
    loads() which restricts map keys and set elements to text strings and
    byte strings in order to prevent denial-of-service attacks via hash
    collisions (GHSA-p6xp-9h6j-r278).
  * Documented decoding concatenated CBOR objects with EOF checks between
    objects.
  * Built Pyodide (pyemscripten) wheels for Python 3.14.
  * Fixed the decoder not rejecting invalid two-byte simple value sequences
    (0xF800 - 0xF81F).
  * Fixed an error in the mutability logic during decoding, leading to
    values being decoded as immutable in unexpected places.
  * Fixed compatibility issues with 32-bit systems.
  * Fixed cbor2.load() returning corrupted data for payloads exceeding 4096
    bytes.
  * Fixed cbor2.load() crash caused by incorrect handling of internal read
    buffer extension during stream deserialization.
  * Fixed incorrect tracking of string references for definite-length text
    strings of length greater than 65536.
  * Fixed the decoder registering 6-byte strings in the string reference
    namespace at indices 65536-4294967295 where the encoder does not,
    desynchronising the namespace.
  * Fixed the IPv4/IPv6 network decoders (tags 52 and 54) silently
    truncating an address byte string that is longer than the address size
    instead of rejecting it as malformed.
  * Fixed frozendict deriving its hash from its keys and its values as two
    independent sets, which caused hash collisions and quadratic-time
    decoding for payloads keyed by such maps.
  * Fixed the encoder not registering bytearray values in the string
    reference namespace, which desynchronised the namespace.
  * Fixed the decoder silently accepting an indefinite-length map whose
    break marker arrives after a key with no value.
  * Fixed the decoder accepting a non-byte-string payload for a positive or
    negative bignum (tags 2 and 3).
  * Fixed CBORSimpleValue hashing inconsistently with the integer it
    compares equal to.
  * Fixed canonical encoding with value sharing enabled emitting shared
    references to container keys that were never written to the stream.
  * Fixed shared references (tag 29) to a map or an unhandled tag resolving
    to the raw dict or CBORTag instead of the value returned by object_hook
    or tag_hook.
  * Fixed the encoder not giving a nested stringref namespace (tag 256) its
    own index space.
  * Fixed the decoder returning its internal break marker as a value when a
    break stop code appeared where a data item was expected.
  * Fixed a PanicException when trying to decode an epoch-form date (tag
    100) with a payload near i32::MAX.
  * Fixed the decoder accepting a string-form datetime (tag 0) without a
    UTC offset and returning a naive datetime instead of rejecting it.
  * Fixed a reused CBOREncoder no longer flushing its output or resetting
    its shared container and string reference tracking after an encode()
    call raised an exception.
  * Fixed CBOREncoder.encode_to_bytes() sharing the string reference
    namespace of the enclosing encode operation when called from a default
    hook.
  * Fixed the encoder writing the repr() of a bytes regular expression
    pattern (tag 35) instead of the pattern itself.
  * Fixed shared references (tag 29) allowing the decoder to construct
    object graphs nested deeper than max_depth, which could crash the
    interpreter with a segmentation fault when hashed
    (GHSA-55vx-2phh-7grr).
  * Fixed missing conversion of date values (tags 100 and 1004) to JSON as
    ISO formatted strings.
  * Fixed a PanicException on Python 3.10 when decoding a string-form
    datetime (tag 0) whose fractional seconds part contains a multi-byte
    Unicode numeric character.
  * Fixed the decoder accepting a set (tag 258) whose payload is not an
    array.
  * Fixed the decoder accepting a non-integer exponent or mantissa in a
    decimal fraction (tag 4) or a bigfloat (tag 5).

